# Lint Before Completing Swift Tasks

Before considering any Swift coding task in this project done, run SwiftLint
with the same flags as the pre-commit hook and resolve every violation:

```bash
DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH=/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/lib \
  swiftlint lint --strict --config .swiftlint.yml
```

- `--strict` treats warnings as failures, matching `.pre-commit-config.yaml`
  so a clean local run means the pre-commit hook will also pass.
- `DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH` is required so SwiftLint's SourceKit loads from the
  Command Line Tools (no Xcode.app installed).
- Fix every reported violation directly (reformat, rename, split lines,
  etc.). Don't add `swiftlint:disable` comments to silence a rule unless it's
  a genuine false positive incompatible with this project's
  ObservableObject/StateObject pattern — see the `disabled_rules` comment in
  `.swiftlint.yml` for the existing precedent and follow the same style of
  justification comment if you add another.
- Also run `swift build` after fixing lint issues to confirm nothing broke.
- Report the final violation count (should be 0) when wrapping up the task.
